WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:12.780
My name is Caucher Birkar. I'm a
professor of mathematics at the

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.679
University of Cambridge.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:25.040
I think it's important to have something
original something authentic both in

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:30.650
mathematics and also generally in life. Because I believe that a lot of problem

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:36.440
in the world, social and political, arise
because people imitate other people,

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:41.540
because countries imitate other
countries. It's okay to learn from others,

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:48.400
to take ideas and to develop it. But it's
not good I think just to imitate others.

00:00:52.629 --> 00:00:57.910
In algebraic geometry, geometric spaces
are called algebraic varieties and some

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:02.409
of them are more special than others.
Especially there are some of them which

00:01:02.409 --> 00:01:07.570
are called final varieties and the one
of the building blocks of algebraic

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:12.970
varieties and what I proved is that if
you put some mild conditions on this

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:18.820
kind of varieties then you can
parameterize them by only finitely many

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:25.149
set of parameters. In a simple
language that just means that you need

00:01:25.149 --> 00:01:31.360
only a fixed set of variables and
equations of a bounded degree to define

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:34.770
all such varieties.

